<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Exchange from '#src/lib/Exchange.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/handlers/clients',
        '/handlers/mcp',
        '/helpers/json-schema',
        '/cli/commands',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/assistant/lib/OpenApiOperation.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the handler is an operation, with its sentence and type'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/generated.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the OpenAPI document publishes what each handler answers — 19.21, 19.22, 19.23, 20.15'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Hand a partner the contact search as an operation">
        <p>Write the handler. Its argument type is the operation's parameters and its
            <code>description</code> is the operation's, with no spec to keep in step.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            // src/assistant/searchContacts.server.ts
            import { rpc } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { CONTACTS } from '../contacts/lib/CONTACTS.server.ts'

            export default rpc(
                ({ name }: { name: string }) =>
                    CONTACTS.filter((contact) => contact.name.includes(name)),
                { description: 'The contacts whose name contains \`name\`.' },
            )
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Read the operation the handler became">
        <p>Fetch <code>/__abide/openapi.json</code> from the running app. The operation's id is
            its method and its route.</p>
        <Code code={`
            $ curl -s localhost:3000/__abide/openapi.json \\
                | jq '.paths["/assistant/searchContacts"].get'
            {
              "operationId": "get_assistant_searchContacts",
              "description": "The contacts whose name contains \`name\`.",
              "parameters": [
                { "name": "name", "in": "query", "required": true,
                  "schema": { "type": "string" } }
              ],
              ...
            }
        `} />
        <p>The CRM's document, asked when this page loaded, with that operation's three fields
            picked out:</p>
        <Exchange
            path="/__abide/openapi.json"
            pick={[
                '/paths/~1assistant~1searchContacts/get/operationId',
                '/paths/~1assistant~1searchContacts/get/description',
                '/paths/~1assistant~1searchContacts/get/parameters',
            ]} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Commit the spec beside the code">
        <p>Print the document from the source, with no server running. Pass
            <code>--url</code> to ask a deployment instead.</p>
        <Code code={`abide openapi > openapi.json`} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
